/**
\page api_type_effectchain EffectChain

An OpenEgg table returned by `Audio.createEffectChain()` or `Audio.getMasterEffectChain()`. It groups child chains, effects, and voices. Retail scripts use it to assemble audio routes; OpenEgg stores the graph locally, but retail DSP processing is not implemented.

| Method | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `addEffect(effectType, parameterPairs...)` | Creates an effect in an available slot and applies optional parameter/value pairs. Returns `SoundEffect` or null. |
| `addEffectChain(child)` | Moves a child chain from its old parent into a free slot. Each chain has 16 child slots. |
| `addVoice(voiceId)` | Routes an active voice through this chain. |
| `freeAllChildEffects()` | Releases effects and makes their slots available again. Each chain has 8 effect slots. |
| `freeAllChildEffectChains()` | Releases unprotected child chains and clears the child slots. |

`Audio.createEffectChain(name)` attaches the new chain to the master chain by default; an optional parent can be supplied. Each parent has 16 child slots. If all are occupied, the new chain is still returned but is not stored in a child slot. `addEffectChain()` has the same slot limit; when full it changes the child’s parent link without storing the child in a slot. `Audio.freeEffectChain()` releases non-master chains. The master chain is protected. Internal keys beginning with `__` are implementation details, not script API fields.

*/

/**
\page api_type_soundeffect SoundEffect

An OpenEgg table returned by `EffectChain.addEffect()`. It stores the selected effect type and local parameter state; it is not a retail DSP object, and audio effect processing is not implemented.

| Method | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `getType()` | Returns the effect type identifier supplied to `addEffect()`. |
| `setBypass(bypass)` | Stores whether bypass is enabled. |
| `setParam(parameterId, value)` | Stores the parameter value after the effect-type-specific conversion. |

`Audio.freeSoundEffect()` releases the effect's owning chain slot. Internal keys beginning with `__` are implementation details, not script API fields.

*/

/**
\page api_type_voiceiterator VoiceIterator

The local table returned by `Audio.getAllVoices()`. It contains a snapshot of voice IDs present when the function is called; later voice changes do not update that snapshot. Ordering is unspecified.

| Method | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `isValid()` | Returns 1 while the current index is within the snapshot, otherwise 0. |
| `get()` | Returns the current voice ID, or null when the index is past the snapshot. |
| `goToNext()` | Advances the index by one and returns no script value. |

Retail scripts use these methods to iterate voices. Retail evidence identifies a native reference-container iterator; OpenEgg currently emulates its script interface with a table, so iterator parity is not verified.

*/

/**
\page api_type_audiosaverequest AudioSaveRequest

The OpenEgg result table returned by `Audio.saveScriptToFile()`. It is separate from `SaveDataTicket` and from the retail asynchronous save-request object.

| Field or method | Type or result | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `size` | int | Compressed file size in bytes when writing succeeds; 0 when serialization, compression, or writing fails. |
| `error` | int | 0 when the save succeeds; 1 when it fails or the requested file area is unsupported. |
| `getSize()` | int | Returns the table's current `size` field. |

Retail scripts use `getSize()` when building level metadata. OpenEgg's V4 recorder format and synchronous write path are local behavior; full retail request-object parity is not verified.

*/

/**
\page api_type_shapevertex SHAPEVERTEX

An OpenEgg proxy returned by `shape.getVertex(index)`. It refers to the indexed vertex in its owning `VMSHAPE`; it is not a detached value or a retail engine object.

| Property | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `x` | number | Vertex x position. |
| `y` | number | Vertex y position. |
| `u` | number | Texture u coordinate. |
| `v` | number | Texture v coordinate. |

Reading or writing a property accesses the owning shape's arrays. Looking up a nonnegative index grows the vertex storage as needed and zero-initializes new values. Assigning an integer or float stores that value; other assigned types become `0`. Unknown property names read as null and ignore writes. The proxy holds a raw pointer to its shape, so only use it while that shape is alive.

*/

/**
\page api_type_savedataticket SaveDataTicket

An OpenEgg compatibility table returned by local save-data request functions. It is not a native GameMonkey type or the retail asynchronous request object. The fields are mutable, and the accessor methods read their current values.

| Field | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `filename` | string | Path associated with the request; empty for constructors without a file path. |
| `size` | int | Reported byte count or requested size, depending on the request function. |
| `done` | int | Completion flag. Current ticket constructors set this to 1. |
| `error` | int | Error flag. `SAVEDATA_reqLoadFile` sets it when the target file is missing; `SAVEDATA_reqSaveString` sets it when writing fails. Other current constructors leave it at 0. |

| Method | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `getSize()` | Returns the `size` field. |
| `getFilename()` | Returns the `filename` field. |
| `getIfDone()` | Returns 1 when `done` is nonzero, otherwise 0. |
| `getIfError()` | Returns 1 when `error` is nonzero, otherwise 0. |

All current constructors set `done` to 1 and return immediately. Retail request-manager timing, failure handling, and ticket lifetime are not verified. `Audio.saveScriptToFile` returns a smaller result table and does not provide all of these fields or methods.

*/
